This directory (apps/sae-text-detector/) is a CPU-only clear-experiment kit for:

  Dugan, McDougall, Denton, Pham, Kaeser-Chen, Callison-Burch,
  "Building Auditable AI Text Detectors with Sparse Autoencoders",
  arXiv:2610.30006 (EMNLP 2026)
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.30006
  https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.30006

Found via a bookmarked X post by @_akhaliq:
  https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2114730846426890689

Official code (used here via the `detectorscope` PyPI package):
  https://github.com/google-deepmind/detectorscope
  License: Apache License 2.0 (copy in LICENSE)

Released Hub detector used at run time (not redistributed in git):
  https://huggingface.co/liamdugan/detector-scope
  - Language model under extractor/: Gemma-2-2b, Gemma Terms of Use
    (https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms) — see the Hub repo NOTICE
  - Sparse autoencoders derive from Gemma Scope (CC-BY-4.0)
  - Heads and feature descriptions: CC-BY-4.0

Dataset used for the clear experiment (downloaded at run time):
  dmitva/human_ai_generated_text — CC-BY-4.0
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/dmitva/human_ai_generated_text

This app's experiment harness, Gradio wrapper, and media scripts are original to
tech-demos. They call the official AuditableDetector API; they are not a
re-implementation of the authors' training pipeline. Results here are a small
CPU slice, not the paper's COLING / RAID tables.

No warranty. Research / demo use. Model weights stay out of git (HF cache /
work/ is git-ignored). No API keys required for the measured run.
